    Declared acts stage 5: a thread is named by its opening act's first text field (request a5d64b35)
    
    The planner's decision c37653e1. A thread with no goal was named by its
    opening act's label and first body field by name. The demo's first field
    by name is an enum, a musical key, so both demo songs were called "Start
    a song: c".
    
    The shared helper titleOf now prefers the first present field by name
    that the act's own declaration, at the act's own seq, types as text.
    With no such field present, or with no declaration at hand (a legacy,
    platform or unknown kind, or a label alone), it is the first field by
    name, as before. A goal still comes first, and the thread's ID is used
    when the opening act is not at hand. No declaration member is added and
    no binding changes.
    
    The UI carries each entry's declaration with its meaning, so that the
    page names a thread with the field types in force when it opened.
    Section 33.10, open point 52, the READMEs and the reader tests of the
    client, CLI, MCP tool and UI are updated together. The browser suite's
    declared-room case now passes to its end.

